# Raw blog hero masters. Blog heroes get iterated as large PNGs (v1, v2, v5...
# routinely 15 to 25MB each) and the chosen one is then exported as a web-sized
# JPG. Only that JPG belongs in the repo. Git keeps every blob forever, so a
# stray 20MB master is permanent weight on every clone and every build; a later
# delete does not undo it.
# Added 2026-08-11 after 54MB of such drafts turned up loose in this folder.
#
# Deliberately scoped to public/images/blog/ only. A blanket
# public/images/**/*.png was drafted first and rejected: 16 PNGs are tracked
# elsewhere under public/images (client logos, and the hero/secondary band
# images for every vertical page), so a blanket rule would silently ignore the
# images of the next vertical page someone builds and ship it broken.
public/images/blog/*.png

